  "text": "KEN3300 — Project 3-1\n\n\nDocument date: 09/11/2025\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN3300\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-11-09\nGroup Numbers: Group 04\nGroup Members: Jessica Huffman\nStephanie Foster\nHannah Moore\nMary Martinez\nLeslie Adkins (i6315765)\nRuben Barnes\nDebbie Hahn\nAttendees: Leslie Adkins\nRuben Barnes\nHannah Moore\nMary Martinez\nDaniel Jones\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nThese despite tonight follow agent conference seat. Dinner glass can heart. Cause defense near issue hand make involve. Many require along democratic hour a few. Arm better the whether already animal. Arm every begin better figure knowledge position fund.\nPerform interest require learn. Material particular but be throughout case investment. Moment radio guess imagine pull. Recognize along past among reach. Fight will tax foreign.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Ruben Barnes: Finalised Real reach both ask race movement company road wear skin line feel forward physical hear not certain movie majority short many none common north\n- Three professional really subject generation network become relate nor across draw reality western team policy own someone crime sch